CRITICAL VIDEO SCRUBNING TECHNIQUE
The video scrubbing uses a requestAnimationFrame loop with a seeking guard — this is the most important performance pattern:

if (!video.seeking && Math.abs(video.currentTime - currentTime) > 0.01) {
  video.currentTime = currentTime;
}

The !video.seeking check is essential. We tell the browser: "Update the video frame ONLY when you have completely finished rendering the previous one." Without this guard, the browser's video decoder gets flooded with seek requests, causing freezing, black frames, and stuttering. The smooth interpolation (currentTime += (targetTime - currentTime) * 0.08) combined with this seeking guard creates a buttery-smooth cinematic scrubbing experience.
